content:
{
  "asset": "Pump P-109, AquaDyne HF-300 end-suction centrifugal pump, serial HF3-23500",
  "priority": "P1",
  "stop_equipment_now": false,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "Drive-end bearing housing temperature is 85 C. The HF-300 limits are normal up to 70 C, alarm at 80 C and trip at 90 C. The reading is 5 C above the alarm limit and 5 C below the trip limit, so it is in the alarm band. The manufacturer's limits apply to housing-surface measurements, which is where the IR gun reading was taken.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C01"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Site standard SSP-07 requires a priority-1 work order within the shift when bearing temperature exceeds the manufacturer's alarm limit. 85 C is above the 80 C alarm, so this work order is P1.",
      "citations": [
        "C15",
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Vibration is 2.5 mm/s. Figure 3 for the HF-300 places this in Zone A (0.0 to 2.8 mm/s RMS, 'New machines'), below the Zone A/B boundary of 2.8 mm/s. It is well below Zone D (7.1 mm/s and above), the only zone that requires an immediate stop.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C06",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "An immediate stop is not required by the evidence. Temperature is below the 90 C trip and vibration is not in the highest severity zone. The pump must still be attended within the shift and watched against the 90 C trip.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "No leakage is reported, so the shaft-seal leakage symptom does not apply and no seal work is indicated at this stage.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [
    {
      "statement": "Over-greasing of the drive-end bearing is the most likely cause. It is listed first for high bearing temperature, and the normal Zone A vibration with no noise does not point to mechanical damage. This ranking is a planner inference from the symptom pattern.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Misalignment is the second candidate. It is a listed cause of high bearing temperature, although the low vibration makes significant misalignment less likely.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Drive-end bearing wear is the third candidate. It is a listed cause of high bearing temperature, but no noise and Zone A vibration argue against advanced wear.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "Within the shift, re-measure drive-end and non-drive-end bearing housing surface temperatures. Monitor the trend against the 80 C alarm and 90 C trip. If 90 C is reached, the trip limit applies.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C01",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Measure vibration velocity on both bearing housings and classify the highest reading using Figure 3. If any reading enters Zone D (7.1 mm/s RMS or more), stop the pump immediately and notify the reliability engineer before restart.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Check the grease quantity in the drive-end bearing (first corrective action for high bearing temperature).",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Check shaft alignment with a laser alignment tool. Tolerances are parallel offset 0.05 mm and angular 0.05 mm per 100 mm. Correct if out of tolerance.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If the bearings show wear, noise or high temperature that persists after the grease and alignment checks, replace both bearings as a pair (5.3): DE HF3-512 (6312-C3) and NDE HF3-510 (6310-C3). Isolate first, apply LOTO, and remove the 68 kg back pull-out assembly under a lifting plan.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C05",
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If the casing is opened, fit a new casing gasket HF3-120.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Only if the mechanical seal is disturbed: fit cartridge seal HF3-450B, not HF3-450, and tighten the seal gland nut to 30 Nm. HF3-450B is pre-set, so no sleeve measurement is needed. Replace shaft sleeve HF3-455 if scoring exceeds 0.1 mm depth.",
      "citations": [
        "C13",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Tighten remaining fasteners to Table 5 of the manual. Table 5 values are not in the evidence; obtain them before starting.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "After any work that moves the motor or the bearing housing, re-align with the laser tool to 0.05 mm parallel and 0.05 mm per 100 mm angular.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "After restart, confirm bearing temperature returns below the 70 C normal limit and vibration remains in Zone A or B.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C07"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-512",
      "description": "Drive-end bearing 6312-C3. Contingency: only if bearing replacement is required; replace as a pair with HF3-510.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-510",
      "description": "Non-drive-end bearing 6310-C3. Contingency: replace as a pair with HF3-512.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-120",
      "description": "Casing gasket. Replace whenever the casing is opened.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-450B",
      "description": "Cartridge mechanical seal, superseding HF3-450 for serial HF3-22000 and above. Contingency: only if the seal is disturbed.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-455",
      "description": "Shaft sleeve. Contingency: only if seal is disturbed and scoring exceeds 0.1 mm depth.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C13",
        "C05"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "Raise and action as a priority-1 work order within the shift, because bearing temperature is above the manufacturer's 80 C alarm limit.",
      "citations": [
        "C15",
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If vibration enters Zone D, stop the machine immediately and notify the reliability engineer before restart.",
      "citations": [
        "C15",
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "For any work inside the pump or on its seal, including bearing replacement via back pull-out, apply the following controls: electrical isolation and LOTO at the MCC; mechanical isolation of the suction and discharge valves; a line-break permit, draining and venting first.",
      "citations": [
        "C15",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The back pull-out assembly weighs 68 kg, which exceeds the 25 kg threshold. A lifting plan signed by the shift supervisor and certified lifting equipment are required.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Never run the pump dry, because the seal flush is Plan 11 from pump discharge. Ensure the pump is primed before restart.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If the line is chemically dosed, wear chemical goggles and nitrile gloves.",
      "citations": [
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [
    {
      "statement": "Laser alignment: 1.5 h, 1 technician.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Bearing replacement (pair), contingency: 6.0 h, 2 technicians, plus 1.5 h laser alignment afterwards.",
      "citations": [
        "C12",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Mechanical seal replacement, contingency only if the seal is disturbed: 4.0 h, 2 technicians.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "The O&M manual (AQ-OM-300 Rev D) lists mechanical seal HF3-450 with fasteners to Table 5. Service bulletin SB-2026-014 (issued 14 March 2026) supersedes this for serials HF3-22000 and above. For those pumps it specifies cartridge seal HF3-450B, gland torque 30 Nm (was 25 Nm), no sleeve measurement, and sleeve replacement if scoring exceeds 0.1 mm. P-109 is serial HF3-23500, which is at or above HF3-22000, so the bulletin applies to this asset. Use HF3-450B at 30 Nm if the seal is touched.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10",
        "C13",
        "C01"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "IR gun accuracy and emissivity setting are not covered. Should the 85 C reading be confirmed with a contact probe?",
    "Is the reported 2.5 mm/s an RMS value, as Figure 3 requires, and was it the highest of both bearing housings?",
    "Correct grease type, quantity and regreasing interval for the 6312-C3 and 6310-C3 bearings are not given in the evidence.",
    "Table 5 fastener torques, other than the 30 Nm seal gland nut from SB-2026-014, are not provided.",
    "Does a laser alignment check alone, without opening the pump, require LOTO under SSP-07? The table only specifies controls for work inside the pump or on its seal.",
    "Does bearing replacement via back pull-out require disturbing the mechanical seal? Section 5.3 does not say.",
    "Is P-109 on a chemically dosed line?",
    "Labour time for the grease quantity check is not listed in Table 6.",
    "Should the 85 C reading and its follow-up be reported to the reliability engineer even though no stop is required? SSP-07 only mandates notification for a Zone D vibration stop."
  ]
}
